<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoMathTrunc</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to implement truncation</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Math.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoValue *SilikoMathTrunc(int argc, SilikoValue **argv);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoMathTrunc</function> truncates the value of
<varname>argv[0]</varname> to the whole-number portion of its
value.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoMathTrunc</function> returns a pointer to an
object representing the result of the truncation function. If
<varname>argc</varname> is not <literal>1</literal>, the returned value
will be an error value with value
<literal>SilikoErrorFunctionArguments</literal>.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Conformance</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoMathTrunc</function> function conforms to SilikoCore’s
interface for pure functions and can be installed into a
<type>SilikoEngine</type> if wrapped with
<function>SilikoPureFunctionCreate</function>.</para>
</refsection>
</refentry>
